Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:20:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Leaf port: walk brain behaviours as flat arrays

Brain#startEachNonRunningBehavior and #tickEachRunningBehavior (and
getRunningBehaviors) iterated the TreeMap of HashMaps of LinkedHashSets of
behaviours on every tick of every brain (villagers, nautilus, ...): that was
about a fifth of Brain.tick in the 12 bot Blitz profile. The behaviours are now
flattened once into (activity, behaviour[]) groups in the exact iteration order
of the old maps and rebuilt whenever behaviours are added or removed. Running
behaviours are still snapshotted before they are ticked, but nothing is
allocated when none runs. The memory slot map is an identity keyed
Reference2ReferenceOpenHashMap (MemoryModuleType has identity semantics) instead
of a HashMap.

Behaviour: identical start/tick order and snapshot semantics; only the
iteration order of the memory map changes, which is only visible in the order
memories are written to NBT.

Adapted from Leaf "Replace brain with optimized collection" (HaHaWTH, Taiyou06
<kaandindar21@gmail.com>, hayanesuru <hayanesuru@outlook.jp>). Leaf also uses
array maps/bit sets keyed by activity id, which changes the behaviour order,
so that part is not ported.
Leaf: https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf

